"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. It was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000 for Phase One, led by Sarah Tan. The project team has expanded multiple times, adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture in September, and later welcoming Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for their expertise in machine learning and cloud computing. A significant budget increase to $2 million was approved by the executive board, with allocations discussed in August. The project has achieved several milestones, including a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, the successful completion of the testing phase, and the establishment of a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and a detailed report on Phase Two progress will be presented on November 20th."
